  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset shows early but concrete uptake: 49 recorded downloads, 236 views, and one documented downstream reuse. It has not yet accumulated OpenAlex citations, so the present record is better read as initial use and visibility rather than established citation impact.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Essential meaning word scores for the GPADS framework is a Zenodo-hosted dataset by Peter Sheridan Dodds that provides tab-separated scores for words across five dimensions of essential meaning: goodness, power, aggression, danger, and structure. The resource sits at the intersection of linguistics, natural language processing, artificial intelligence, psychology, and mathematical approaches to meaning, reflecting its role as a measurement tool for semantic analysis rather than a conventional article advancing a single empirical result.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of impact in the current record comes from usage and reuse. Datacite reports 236 views and 49 downloads, indicating that the dataset has already drawn attention from readers who went beyond a casual look. In addition, the reuse graph documents one downstream reuse, including a biomedical article mention, which is a meaningful sign that the dataset is being incorporated into other scholarly work.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citation record is still sparse. OpenAlex currently shows 0 citations, and scite reports one mentioning citation with no supporting or contradicting citations recorded. Together, these signals suggest that the dataset is visible and has begun to circulate, but that its longer-term scholarly citation footprint has not yet developed in the available indexes.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Stewardship and access are strong features of the record. The dataset is deposited in Zenodo, an open repository with DOI-based persistence, and repository matching shows both the original record and linked versions. The work also has a WorldCat holdings signal, which may aid discoverability in library and instructional contexts, though the record does not itself establish teaching adoption.</p>",
